{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Hear, O Israel.</b> Even if you have no merit but the recitation of Shema alone, you are worthy that He save you." "<b>Against your enemies.</b> These are not your brothers — for if you fall into their hands they do not show you mercy. This is not like the war of Judah with Israel, of which it is said (II Chronicles 28:15), ״And the men who were designated by name arose and took hold of the captives, and all who were naked among them they clothed from the spoil, and they clothed them and shod them and fed them and gave them drink and anointed them, and led them on donkeys to every feeble one, and brought them to Jericho, the city of palms, to their brothers, and they returned to Samaria״ — but against your enemies you go; therefore strengthen yourselves for battle (Sifrei; Sotah 42)." "<b>Let your heart not be faint, do not fear, do not panic, do not be broken.</b> Four warnings corresponding to four things that the kings of the nations do: they clash their shields together to strike one against the other, to make a sound so that those opposite will panic and flee; and they gallop their horses and make them prance to make a sound of the stamping of their horses' hooves; and they shout with their voices; and they blow the shofarot and other instruments that make sound." "<b>Let your heart not be faint.</b> From the neighing of horses." "<b>Do not fear.</b> From the clashing of shields." "<b>And do not panic.</b> At the sound of the horns." "<b>And do not be terrified.</b> At the sound of the shouting (there [in that verse])."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:48.687354917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}